-- Sale of Goods Act 1979 (Singapore).  LAYER 1 TESTS for Part 3 (ss 16 to 26).
-- Expected values are written from the text beside each assertion, before running.
-- Argument lists follow the GIVEN order of the rule called.  Dates are Date day month year.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `soga-nouns`
IMPORT `soga-part3-effects`

-- s 16: unascertained goods, not yet ascertained: no property passes (subject to s 20A).
#ASSERT `s 16 property in unascertained goods is transferred to the buyer` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 16 property in unascertained goods is transferred to the buyer` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- ascertained: ss 17 and 18 decide
#ASSERT `s 16 property in unascertained goods is transferred to the buyer` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- s 20A
#ASSERT `s 16 property in unascertained goods is transferred to the buyer` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not unascertained goods
-- s 16, the bar (ruling (d) of 2026-11-05 applied to the same words; assumed, not ruled): arguments are the contract is for unascertained goods, the goods are ascertained, section 20A applies.
#ASSERT `s 16 property in unascertained goods cannot yet be transferred` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- unascertained goods, not yet ascertained: barred
#ASSERT `s 16 property in unascertained goods cannot yet be transferred` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- ascertained: the bar is spent
#ASSERT `s 16 property in unascertained goods cannot yet be transferred` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not a contract for unascertained goods: the "where" is unmet, no bar
#ASSERT `s 16 property in unascertained goods cannot yet be transferred` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- s 20A applies: subject to that section
-- s 17(1): the parties' intended time.
#ASSERT `s 17(1) the time at which the property in the goods is transferred to the buyer` TRUE (JUST (Date 1 4 2025)) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 4 2025)
#ASSERT `s 17(1) the time at which the property in the goods is transferred to the buyer` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 17(1) the time at which the property in the goods is transferred to the buyer` FALSE (JUST (Date 1 4 2025)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 17(2): sources of evidence.
#ASSERT `s 17(2) regard shall be had to this source in ascertaining the intention of the parties` `the terms of the contract` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17(2) regard shall be had to this source in ascertaining the intention of the parties` `the conduct of the parties` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17(2) regard shall be had to this source in ascertaining the intention of the parties` `the circumstances of the case` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 17(2) regard shall be had to this source in ascertaining the intention of the parties` `something else` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 18 chapeau.
#ASSERT `s 18 the following are rules for ascertaining the intention of the parties as to when the property passes` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18 the following are rules for ascertaining the intention of the parties as to when the property passes` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 18(a) Rule 1: unconditional contract, specific goods, deliverable state: property passes when the contract is made (10 March 2025).
#ASSERT `s 18(a) Rule 1: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 10 3 2025) (Date 10 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- on the day the contract is made
#ASSERT `s 18(a) Rule 1: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 10 3 2025) (Date 9 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the day before: no contract yet
#ASSERT `s 18(a) Rule 1: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 10 3 2025) (Date 30 6 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- later, though payment or delivery is postponed
#ASSERT `s 18(a) Rule 1: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 10 3 2025) (Date 30 6 2025) EQUALS NOTHING -- a different intention appears
#ASSERT `s 18(a) Rule 1: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` FALSE FALSE TRUE (Date 10 3 2025) (Date 30 6 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a conditional contract
#ASSERT `s 18(a) Rule 1: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` FALSE TRUE FALSE (Date 10 3 2025) (Date 30 6 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not in a deliverable state
-- s 18(b) Rule 2: seller bound to do something to put the goods into a deliverable state; done 5 March, notice 8 March 2025.
#ASSERT `s 18(b) Rule 2: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST (Date 5 3 2025)) (JUST (Date 8 3 2025)) (Date 7 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- done but no notice yet
#ASSERT `s 18(b) Rule 2: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST (Date 5 3 2025)) (JUST (Date 8 3 2025)) (Date 8 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING -- done and notice: the rule is silent on passing
#ASSERT `s 18(b) Rule 2: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` FALSE TRUE TRUE NOTHING NOTHING (Date 8 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not done
#ASSERT `s 18(b) Rule 2: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST (Date 9 3 2025)) (JUST (Date 8 3 2025)) (Date 8 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- done only after the date asked about
#ASSERT `s 18(b) Rule 2: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING NOTHING (Date 8 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING -- a different intention appears
#ASSERT `s 18(b) Rule 2: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` FALSE TRUE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING (Date 8 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the seller is not bound to do anything
-- s 18(c) Rule 3: act with reference to the goods for ascertaining the price; done 5 March, notice 8 March 2025.
#ASSERT `s 18(c) Rule 3: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST (Date 5 3 2025)) (JUST (Date 8 3 2025)) (Date 7 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18(c) Rule 3: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST (Date 5 3 2025)) (JUST (Date 8 3 2025)) (Date 8 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 18(c) Rule 3: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` FALSE TRUE TRUE NOTHING (JUST (Date 8 3 2025)) (Date 8 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- act not done
#ASSERT `s 18(c) Rule 3: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING NOTHING (Date 8 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 18(c) Rule 3: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` FALSE FALSE TRUE NOTHING NOTHING (Date 8 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not a deliverable-state contract
-- s 18(b) Rule 2, the bar (ruled 2026-11-05): JUST TRUE until the thing is done and the buyer has notice, JUST FALSE from then on and where the rule does not apply.
#ASSERT `s 18(b) Rule 2: the property cannot yet pass` FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST (Date 5 3 2025)) (JUST (Date 8 3 2025)) (Date 7 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- done, no notice yet: still barred
#ASSERT `s 18(b) Rule 2: the property cannot yet pass` FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST (Date 5 3 2025)) (JUST (Date 8 3 2025)) (Date 8 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- done and notice by the day asked about: no longer barred
#ASSERT `s 18(b) Rule 2: the property cannot yet pass` FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST (Date 5 3 2025)) (JUST (Date 8 3 2025)) (Date 9 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the day after: still not barred
#ASSERT `s 18(b) Rule 2: the property cannot yet pass` FALSE TRUE TRUE NOTHING NOTHING (Date 8 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the thing is not done
#ASSERT `s 18(b) Rule 2: the property cannot yet pass` FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST (Date 9 3 2025)) (JUST (Date 8 3 2025)) (Date 8 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- done only after the day asked about
#ASSERT `s 18(b) Rule 2: the property cannot yet pass` FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST (Date 5 3 2025)) NOTHING (Date 8 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- done but the buyer has no notice
#ASSERT `s 18(b) Rule 2: the property cannot yet pass` TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING NOTHING (Date 8 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a different intention appears: the rule is displaced, no bar
#ASSERT `s 18(b) Rule 2: the property cannot yet pass` TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST (Date 5 3 2025)) (JUST (Date 8 3 2025)) (Date 7 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a different intention appears, even before the notice
#ASSERT `s 18(b) Rule 2: the property cannot yet pass` FALSE FALSE TRUE NOTHING NOTHING (Date 8 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not a contract for specific goods: the "where" is unmet, no bar
#ASSERT `s 18(b) Rule 2: the property cannot yet pass` FALSE TRUE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING (Date 8 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the seller is not bound to do anything: no bar
-- The two together, on the same facts (done 5 March, notice 8 March, asked 8 March): the bar answers JUST FALSE (the second bar assertion above), and the function `s 18(b) Rule 2: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` answers NOTHING (the assertion "done and notice: the rule is silent on passing" above). The bar is spent; the text still does not say the property has passed.
-- s 18(c) Rule 3, the bar (ruled 2026-11-05).
#ASSERT `s 18(c) Rule 3: the property cannot yet pass` FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST (Date 5 3 2025)) (JUST (Date 8 3 2025)) (Date 7 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- done, no notice yet: still barred
#ASSERT `s 18(c) Rule 3: the property cannot yet pass` FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST (Date 5 3 2025)) (JUST (Date 8 3 2025)) (Date 8 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- done and notice by the day asked about: no longer barred
#ASSERT `s 18(c) Rule 3: the property cannot yet pass` FALSE TRUE TRUE NOTHING (JUST (Date 8 3 2025)) (Date 8 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the act is not done
#ASSERT `s 18(c) Rule 3: the property cannot yet pass` FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST (Date 9 3 2025)) (JUST (Date 8 3 2025)) (Date 8 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- done only after the day asked about
#ASSERT `s 18(c) Rule 3: the property cannot yet pass` TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING NOTHING (Date 8 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a different intention appears: no bar
#ASSERT `s 18(c) Rule 3: the property cannot yet pass` FALSE FALSE TRUE NOTHING NOTHING (Date 8 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not a deliverable-state contract: the "where" is unmet, no bar
#ASSERT `s 18(c) Rule 3: the property cannot yet pass` FALSE TRUE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING (Date 8 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the seller is not bound to weigh or measure: no bar
-- s 18(d) Rule 4: goods on approval or sale or return.
#ASSERT `s 18(d) Rule 4: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` FALSE TRUE (JUST (Date 5 3 2025)) FALSE FALSE (Date 20 3 2025) (Date 10 4 2025) (Date 5 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (i): he signifies approval on 5 March
#ASSERT `s 18(d) Rule 4: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` FALSE TRUE (JUST (Date 5 3 2025)) FALSE FALSE (Date 20 3 2025) (Date 10 4 2025) (Date 4 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the day before
#ASSERT `s 18(d) Rule 4: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` FALSE TRUE NOTHING TRUE TRUE (Date 20 3 2025) (Date 10 4 2025) (Date 20 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (ii): retains without notice of rejection; the fixed time expires on 20 March
#ASSERT `s 18(d) Rule 4: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` FALSE TRUE NOTHING TRUE TRUE (Date 20 3 2025) (Date 10 4 2025) (Date 19 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the day before the fixed time expires
#ASSERT `s 18(d) Rule 4: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` FALSE TRUE NOTHING TRUE FALSE (Date 20 3 2025) (Date 10 4 2025) (Date 10 4 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- no time fixed: a reasonable time expires on 10 April
#ASSERT `s 18(d) Rule 4: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` FALSE TRUE NOTHING TRUE FALSE (Date 20 3 2025) (Date 10 4 2025) (Date 9 4 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18(d) Rule 4: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` FALSE TRUE NOTHING FALSE TRUE (Date 20 3 2025) (Date 10 4 2025) (Date 30 6 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- he gave notice of rejection
#ASSERT `s 18(d) Rule 4: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` FALSE FALSE (JUST (Date 5 3 2025)) FALSE FALSE (Date 20 3 2025) (Date 10 4 2025) (Date 30 6 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not on approval
#ASSERT `s 18(d) Rule 4: the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` TRUE TRUE (JUST (Date 5 3 2025)) FALSE FALSE (Date 20 3 2025) (Date 10 4 2025) (Date 30 6 2025) EQUALS NOTHING -- a different intention appears
-- s 18(e)(i) Rule 5(i): unconditional appropriation with assent on 12 March 2025.
#ASSERT `s 18(e)(i) Rule 5(i): the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 12 3 2025) (Date 12 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18(e)(i) Rule 5(i): the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 12 3 2025) (Date 11 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18(e)(i) Rule 5(i): the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 12 3 2025) (Date 13 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- no assent
#ASSERT `s 18(e)(i) Rule 5(i): the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 12 3 2025) (Date 13 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not unconditionally appropriated
#ASSERT `s 18(e)(i) Rule 5(i): the property in the goods has passed to the buyer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 12 3 2025) (Date 13 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 18(e)(ii) Rule 5(ii).
#ASSERT `s 18(e)(ii) Rule 5(ii): the seller is taken to have unconditionally appropriated the goods to the contract` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18(e)(ii) Rule 5(ii): the seller is taken to have unconditionally appropriated the goods to the contract` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- right of disposal reserved
#ASSERT `s 18(e)(ii) Rule 5(ii): the seller is taken to have unconditionally appropriated the goods to the contract` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 18(e)(iii) Rule 5(iii): bulk reduced on 15 March 2025.
#ASSERT `s 18(e)(iii) Rule 5(iii): the remaining goods are appropriated and the property has passed to the buyer` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 15 3 2025) (Date 15 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18(e)(iii) Rule 5(iii): the remaining goods are appropriated and the property has passed to the buyer` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 15 3 2025) (Date 14 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18(e)(iii) Rule 5(iii): the remaining goods are appropriated and the property has passed to the buyer` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 15 3 2025) (Date 16 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- another buyer is owed goods
#ASSERT `s 18(e)(iii) Rule 5(iii): the remaining goods are appropriated and the property has passed to the buyer` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 15 3 2025) (Date 16 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- bulk not reduced
#ASSERT `s 18(e)(iii) Rule 5(iii): the remaining goods are appropriated and the property has passed to the buyer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 15 3 2025) (Date 16 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 18(e)(iv) Rule 5(iv).
#ASSERT `s 18(e)(iv) Rule 5(iv): the property in the remaining goods has passed to the single buyer` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 15 3 2025) (Date 15 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 18(e)(iv) Rule 5(iv): the property in the remaining goods has passed to the single buyer` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 15 3 2025) (Date 14 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18(e)(iv) Rule 5(iv): the property in the remaining goods has passed to the single buyer` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 15 3 2025) (Date 16 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18(e)(iv) Rule 5(iv): the property in the remaining goods has passed to the single buyer` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 15 3 2025) (Date 16 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18(e)(iv) Rule 5(iv): the property in the remaining goods has passed to the single buyer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 15 3 2025) (Date 16 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 19(1).
#ASSERT `s 19(1) the property in the goods passes to the buyer` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- right of disposal reserved, conditions not fulfilled, even though delivered
#ASSERT `s 19(1) the property in the goods passes to the buyer` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- conditions fulfilled: the subsection says only when it does not pass
#ASSERT `s 19(1) the property in the goods passes to the buyer` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- nothing reserved
#ASSERT `s 19(1) the property in the goods passes to the buyer` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 19(1), the bar (ruling (d) of 2026-11-05 applied to the same words; assumed, not ruled): arguments are the contract is for specific or appropriated goods, the seller reserved the right of disposal, the conditions are fulfilled.
#ASSERT `s 19(1) the property cannot yet pass because the right of disposal is reserved` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- reserved, conditions not fulfilled, even though delivered: barred
#ASSERT `s 19(1) the property cannot yet pass because the right of disposal is reserved` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- conditions fulfilled: the bar is spent
#ASSERT `s 19(1) the property cannot yet pass because the right of disposal is reserved` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- nothing reserved: no bar
#ASSERT `s 19(1) the property cannot yet pass because the right of disposal is reserved` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not a contract of the kind the subsection names: the "where" is unmet, no bar
-- s 19(2).
#ASSERT `s 19(2) the seller is taken to reserve the right of disposal` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 19(2) the seller is taken to reserve the right of disposal` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- prima facie only
#ASSERT `s 19(2) the seller is taken to reserve the right of disposal` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 19(3).
#ASSERT `s 19(3) the buyer is bound to return the bill of lading` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 19(3) the buyer is bound to return the bill of lading` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- he honoured the bill of exchange
#ASSERT `s 19(3) the buyer is bound to return the bill of lading` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 19(3) the property in the goods passes to the buyer` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 19(3) the property in the goods passes to the buyer` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 19(3) the property in the goods passes to the buyer` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 20(1): risk follows property unless otherwise agreed.
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the party at whose risk the goods are` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST Seller
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the party at whose risk the goods are` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST Buyer -- whether delivery has been made or not
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the party at whose risk the goods are` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the party at whose risk the goods are` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 20(2): delay through the fault of one party.
#ASSERT `s 20(2) the party at whose risk the goods are as regards the loss` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST Buyer
#ASSERT `s 20(2) the party at whose risk the goods are as regards the loss` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST Seller
#ASSERT `s 20(2) the party at whose risk the goods are as regards the loss` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 20(2) the party at whose risk the goods are as regards the loss` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- loss would have occurred anyway
#ASSERT `s 20(2) the party at whose risk the goods are as regards the loss` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 20(3).
#ASSERT `s 20(3) section 20 affects the duties or liabilities of the seller or buyer as a bailee or custodier` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20(3) section 20 affects the duties or liabilities of the seller or buyer as a bailee or custodier` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 20A(1).
#ASSERT `s 20A(1) section 20A applies to the contract` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20A(1) section 20A applies to the contract` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20A(1) section 20A applies to the contract` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- bulk not identified
#ASSERT `s 20A(1) section 20A applies to the contract` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the buyer has not paid
-- s 20A(2).
#ASSERT `s 20A(2) property in an undivided share in the bulk is transferred to the buyer and he becomes an owner in common` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20A(2) property in an undivided share in the bulk is transferred to the buyer and he becomes an owner in common` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20A(2) property in an undivided share in the bulk is transferred to the buyer and he becomes an owner in common` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20A(2) the time at which property in the undivided share is transferred` (Date 1 3 2025) NOTHING EQUALS Date 1 3 2025 -- as soon as the conditions are met
#ASSERT `s 20A(2) the time at which property in the undivided share is transferred` (Date 1 3 2025) (JUST (Date 15 3 2025)) EQUALS Date 15 3 2025 -- a later time the parties agree
#ASSERT `s 20A(2) the time at which property in the undivided share is transferred` (Date 1 3 2025) (JUST (Date 20 2 2025)) EQUALS Date 1 3 2025 -- an earlier agreed date is not "a later time"
-- s 20A(3): share = quantity paid for and due / quantity in the bulk.
#ASSERT `s 20A(3) the undivided share of the buyer in the bulk` 30 100 EQUALS JUST 0.3
#ASSERT `s 20A(3) the undivided share of the buyer in the bulk` 30 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 20A(4): reduce proportionately if the shares together exceed the whole.
#ASSERT `s 20A(4) the undivided share of this buyer after proportionate reduction` 0.6 1.2 EQUALS 0.5
#ASSERT `s 20A(4) the undivided share of this buyer after proportionate reduction` 0.6 1 EQUALS 0.6 -- exactly the whole: no reduction
#ASSERT `s 20A(4) the undivided share of this buyer after proportionate reduction` 0.6 0.8 EQUALS 0.6
-- s 20A(5): a delivery is ascribed first to the goods paid for.
#ASSERT `s 20A(5) the quantity of paid-for goods still to be delivered after the delivery` 10 4 EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `s 20A(5) the quantity of paid-for goods still to be delivered after the delivery` 10 10 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 20A(5) the quantity of paid-for goods still to be delivered after the delivery` 10 12 EQUALS 0
-- s 20A(6): part payment of the price is payment for a corresponding part of the goods.
#ASSERT `s 20A(6) the quantity of goods treated as paid for` 40 25 100 EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `s 20A(6) the quantity of goods treated as paid for` 40 25 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 20B(1).
#ASSERT `s 20B(1) the owner in common is deemed to have consented to the dealing` TRUE `a delivery out of the bulk to another owner in common of goods due to him under his contract` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20B(1) the owner in common is deemed to have consented to the dealing` TRUE `a dealing, removal, delivery or disposal of goods in the bulk by another owner in common, within that co-owner's undivided share at the time` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20B(1) the owner in common is deemed to have consented to the dealing` TRUE `some other dealing with the bulk` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 20B(1) the owner in common is deemed to have consented to the dealing` FALSE `a delivery out of the bulk to another owner in common of goods due to him under his contract` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 20B(2).
#ASSERT `s 20B(2) a cause of action accrues to anyone against the person who so acted` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20B(2) a cause of action accrues to anyone against the person who so acted` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 20B(3).
#ASSERT `s 20B(3) section 20A or 20B imposes or affects the matter` `an obligation on a buyer out of a bulk to compensate another buyer for a shortfall` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20B(3) section 20A or 20B imposes or affects the matter` `a contractual arrangement between buyers for adjustments between themselves` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20B(3) section 20A or 20B imposes or affects the matter` `the rights of a buyer under his contract` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20B(3) section 20A or 20B imposes or affects the matter` `some other matter under section 20A or 20B` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 21(1).
#ASSERT `s 21(1) the buyer acquires a better title to the goods than the seller had` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21(1) the buyer acquires a better title to the goods than the seller had` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- the owner is precluded by his conduct
#ASSERT `s 21(1) the buyer acquires a better title to the goods than the seller had` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- sold with the owner's authority
#ASSERT `s 21(1) the buyer acquires a better title to the goods than the seller had` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the seller is the owner
-- s 21(2).
#ASSERT `s 21(2) this Act affects the matter` `the provisions of the Factors Act 1889 or an enactment enabling the apparent owner of goods to dispose of them as if he were their true owner` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21(2) this Act affects the matter` `the validity of a contract of sale under a special common law or statutory power of sale or under the order of a court of competent jurisdiction` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 21(2) this Act affects the matter` `some other matter under section 21(2)` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 23.
#ASSERT `s 23 the buyer acquires a good title to the goods` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23 the buyer acquires a good title to the goods` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not in good faith
#ASSERT `s 23 the buyer acquires a good title to the goods` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- with notice of the defect
#ASSERT `s 23 the buyer acquires a good title to the goods` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the seller's title had already been avoided
#ASSERT `s 23 the buyer acquires a good title to the goods` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the seller's title was not voidable
-- s 24 and s 25.
#ASSERT `s 24 the delivery or transfer has the same effect as if the seller were expressly authorised by the owner to make it` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 24 the delivery or transfer has the same effect as if the seller were expressly authorised by the owner to make it` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 24 the delivery or transfer has the same effect as if the seller were expressly authorised by the owner to make it` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 24 the delivery or transfer has the same effect as if the seller were expressly authorised by the owner to make it` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not in good faith
#ASSERT `s 24 the delivery or transfer has the same effect as if the seller were expressly authorised by the owner to make it` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- notice of the previous sale
